description:
Build reusable test utilities that don't rely on mocks.

## Utilities to Create

### Frame Comparison
```rust
/// Compare two frames with configurable tolerance
pub fn assert_frames_similar(a: &Frame, b: &Frame, tolerance: f32);

/// Compare frame dimensions and format only
pub fn assert_frame_metadata_eq(a: &Frame, b: &Frame);

/// Calculate PSNR between two frames
pub fn frame_psnr(a: &Frame, b: &Frame) -> f32;
```

### Timing Assertions
```rust
/// Assert operation completes within duration
pub fn assert_completes_within<F, T>(f: F, max_duration: Duration) -> T;

/// Measure and log operation duration
pub fn timed<F, T>(name: &str, f: F) -> (T, Duration);
```

### State Assertions
```rust
/// Assert state machine transitions correctly
pub fn assert_valid_transition(from: AppState, to: AppState);

/// Wait for state with timeout
pub async fn wait_for_state(sm: &StateMachine, target: AppState, timeout: Duration);
```

### Error Assertions
```rust
/// Assert error has expected severity
pub fn assert_error_severity(err: &MicroundError, expected: ErrorSeverity);

/// Assert error message contains expected text
pub fn assert_error_contains(err: &MicroundError, text: &str);
```

## File Location
tests/common/assertions.rs - shared across all test modules

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All utilities compile and pass self-tests
- [ ] No mock dependencies
- [ ] Detailed logging in each utility
- [ ] Documentation with examples
